From 0e6962fc07b1d3adc1273f1176da74b4eb7c325f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christopher A. Williamson" <contact@chrisaw.io>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:58:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 22/33] remove aiseal and npu framework clients

neither the aiseal host service nor the npu manager service exists on
the gsi: both mainline modules are flag-disabled and their system
features are never declared, so the client classes, the
AiSealSystemService library and both SystemServer start blocks are
dead weight. drop them along with their SystemServiceRegistry
registrations and the android.aiseal api surface entries. the aconfig
flag declarations stay because Context and PackageManager feature and
service constants still carry FlaggedApi annotations on them, and the
manifest permission definitions stay because the shell package
requests one of them.
